course: dictionary
lesson: 15995
title: Vacant: empty and free
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Vacant means empty, or not being used by anyone. «The vacant seat next to Mia was the only free place on the bus.» Nobody is sitting in it, so vacant means empty.
explain: A vacant job is one that nobody is doing yet, so someone could be hired for it. Hotels use the same idea: a sign that says «Vacancies» means rooms are free for guests. Try swapping in empty: does the sentence still make sense?
explain: Vacant can also describe a look on someone's face. «Sam gave a vacant stare at the board.» His eyes are open, but no thought is in them, as if he is not paying attention. Look at the words around the word to find its meaning.
fact: Vacant is an adjective, and the adverb vacantly describes doing something with an empty, blank look.
fact: «The vacant house has nobody living in it.» Vacant means empty and not lived in.
fact: «The café has a vacant job for a cook.» A vacant job is one that nobody is doing yet.
fact: «A vacant stare» shows no thought or interest, and can show tiredness or shock.
fact: Vacancies (plural) means empty places, such as free rooms at a hotel or jobs waiting to be filled.
exercise: «The vacant seat was at the back of the bus.» What does vacant mean here? | Broken and dirty | Very crowded | *Empty, with nobody sitting in it | Full of people waiting to get on
exercise: A hotel sign says «Vacancies». What does it mean? | The hotel has a swimming pool | *Rooms are free for guests | The hotel is closed for cleaning | All the rooms are full
exercise: «Ella gave a vacant stare at the clock.» What does vacant suggest? | She was very hungry | *Her mind was somewhere else, with no thought in her eyes | She was reading the clock carefully | She was very angry and shouting
test: «The vacant lot next to the school is full of weeds.» What is a vacant lot? | A shop that sells lots of food | A lot of cars parked in neat rows | *An empty piece of land | A building with many floors
test: «The café has a vacant job for a cook.» What does this mean? | The cook has gone on holiday | The café is closed forever | *Nobody is doing the cook's job yet | The cook is very busy
exam: A bus has 40 seats and 27 are taken. How many seats are vacant? | 67 | 27 | *13 | 14
